  "baselines": "HOTA: V7f is significantly above the stronger simple baseline (OTSU-2) in C3, C4, C5 (+3.09, +2.29, +2.74) and not significantly different in C1 (-0.52 [-1.51, +0.09]). MOTA: OTSU-2 is significantly higher than V7f in C1 (-2.85) and C4 (-4.24); V7f higher in C3 (+2.75); C5 n.s. In C4 V7f also has lower MOTA than the host (49.97 vs 54.41).",
  "ablation": "HOTA (C1/C3/C4/C5): the continuation rescue matters for OC-SORT (-3.34, -1.16 without it); the mode decision matters on the RT-DETR-L and halved-score cells (always clean: -0.90, -2.40, -2.44); remap helps under halved scores (-1.67, -0.61 without it) but costs 0.39 on C1; motion tolerance, background check and the duplicate rule change HOTA by at most 0.15 on KITTI; always noisy is within -0.19..+0.85 of V7f on KITTI (its cost on strong MOT17 trackers is the AOB result, Table 7)."
